{
  "dom_id": "step-q316909",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "In rectangle $ABCD,$ $AB=10$ and $BC=6\\sqrt{2}.$ Find the **exact** value of $|\\overset{\\to }{BD}|.$\n\n$|\\overset{\\to }{BD}|=$\n {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251078/assets/537669ec91bb6fd620d64816d4ccf0e0a5c403aa8ba6e03c8fb89c8d71785d24.png)\n\nAs we can see from the picture above, in $△BAD$ we have $m∠BAD={90}^{∘},$ $AB=10,$ and $AD=BC=6\\sqrt{2}.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{BD}| & =BD \\\\  & =\\sqrt{A{B}^{2}+A{D}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{10}^{2}+(6\\sqrt{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100+72} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{172} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{43}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $|\\overset{\\to }{BD}|=2\\sqrt{43}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
